1283b6db-b266-5d77-a129-b29326dc0d71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1283b6db-b266-5d77-a129-b29326dc0d71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1283b6db-b266-5d77-a129-b29326dc0d71" :answer/id #uuid "1283b6db-b266-5d77-a129-b29326dc0d71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd7a500f-046f-5893-90a4-f59a988d6289" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd7a500f-046f-5893-90a4-f59a988d6289" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-18993b3f-5683-5719-85ee-13326dfe87b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18993b3f-5683-5719-85ee-13326dfe87b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18993b3f-5683-5719-85ee-13326dfe87b0" :answer/id #uuid "18993b3f-5683-5719-85ee-13326dfe87b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\cos(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-56051b19-45b1-5fa8-8a80-fcf04ced3c57" :answer-field/id #uuid "56051b19-45b1-5fa8-8a80-fcf04ced3c57" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bf9b7878-8800-5bfd-958d-ab5073eb80a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf9b7878-8800-5bfd-958d-ab5073eb80a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf9b7878-8800-5bfd-958d-ab5073eb80a3" :answer/id #uuid "bf9b7878-8800-5bfd-958d-ab5073eb80a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cos(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97947e83-7ebd-5c1a-b00d-74670b863241" :answer-field/id #uuid "97947e83-7ebd-5c1a-b00d-74670b863241" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cb919bb0-5556-5c1f-93e6-5c26550bd5b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb919bb0-5556-5c1f-93e6-5c26550bd5b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb919bb0-5556-5c1f-93e6-5c26550bd5b7" :answer/id #uuid "cb919bb0-5556-5c1f-93e6-5c26550bd5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129199 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72611a88-9d34-5676-b505-ea5928bf6c8a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-72611a88-9d34-5676-b505-ea5928bf6c8a" :question/id #uuid "72611a88-9d34-5676-b505-ea5928bf6c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-83500" :question/problem "![](images/55/55bbf6f55ce287321f2cc593ea48d65a78c655ca18d2a34df68b63c2bda92c8f.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the semicircle shown above. What is\n${∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A$\nexpressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ))\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75ea2526-b966-5bc2-949f-e2b7d5c9deed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75ea2526-b966-5bc2-949f-e2b7d5c9deed" :answer-field/id #uuid "75ea2526-b966-5bc2-949f-e2b7d5c9deed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb339401-80d8-5441-8a36-c4eb7250cbc0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-545b4aad-bc8c-59f4-a624-a099157d5076" "answer-adfa686a-3a9f-5c43-baff-2feb8fd0100f" "answer-8930c666-998a-5367-8dd0-b9dfcc9f93f4" "answer-cb339401-80d8-5441-8a36-c4eb7250cbc0" "answer-cfda085a-1d8b-55be-bd0f-4cfdeac71375"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-545b4aad-bc8c-59f4-a624-a099157d5076" :answer/id #uuid "545b4aad-bc8c-59f4-a624-a099157d5076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adfa686a-3a9f-5c43-baff-2feb8fd0100f" :answer/id #uuid "adfa686a-3a9f-5c43-baff-2feb8fd0100f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8930c666-998a-5367-8dd0-b9dfcc9f93f4" :answer/id #uuid "8930c666-998a-5367-8dd0-b9dfcc9f93f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb339401-80d8-5441-8a36-c4eb7250cbc0" :answer/id #uuid "cb339401-80d8-5441-8a36-c4eb7250cbc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfda085a-1d8b-55be-bd0f-4cfdeac71375" :answer/id #uuid "cfda085a-1d8b-55be-bd0f-4cfdeac71375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129278 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47812564-3d50-5e9e-a030-d910fa667ee9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-47812564-3d50-5e9e-a030-d910fa667ee9" :question/id #uuid "47812564-3d50-5e9e-a030-d910fa667ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161606" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ for $x\\ge 0,$ $y\\ge 0$ and between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=y+3.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/b6/b6bf808437f48af8b0853108079bde0577c92812ebf868d04a0550ecacb3376e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y+3=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z\\le r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta [z]_{z=0}^{z=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +12{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +12{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +4{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]}_{r=0}^{r=2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +4(2)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +32\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =[-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +32\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]_{\\theta =0}^{\\theta =\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(-1-1)+32(1-0)) \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f69e9c6d-9eea-5554-8872-d044f41b5762"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f69e9c6d-9eea-5554-8872-d044f41b5762" :answer-field/id #uuid "f69e9c6d-9eea-5554-8872-d044f41b5762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74f3c49e-b5f3-5c5e-b0db-c523644cd561" :answer-field/choices ["answer-012fa540-5e42-507c-b4d7-4be584a8a37c" "answer-de2d26a9-566a-53ef-8878-c12a27c0ec9d" "answer-d2fa903f-cfe5-50db-9712-2e6a3f05be62" "answer-74f3c49e-b5f3-5c5e-b0db-c523644cd561" "answer-6ca03990-4e3c-545a-89cf-a853738bd60a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-012fa540-5e42-507c-b4d7-4be584a8a37c" :answer/id #uuid "012fa540-5e42-507c-b4d7-4be584a8a37c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de2d26a9-566a-53ef-8878-c12a27c0ec9d" :answer/id #uuid "de2d26a9-566a-53ef-8878-c12a27c0ec9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2fa903f-cfe5-50db-9712-2e6a3f05be62" :answer/id #uuid "d2fa903f-cfe5-50db-9712-2e6a3f05be62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74f3c49e-b5f3-5c5e-b0db-c523644cd561" :answer/id #uuid "74f3c49e-b5f3-5c5e-b0db-c523644cd561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca03990-4e3c-545a-89cf-a853738bd60a" :answer/id #uuid "6ca03990-4e3c-545a-89cf-a853738bd60a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d807e12-6960-57f6-b74d-aa3fe66f0f76"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d807e12-6960-57f6-b74d-aa3fe66f0f76" :question/id #uuid "8d807e12-6960-57f6-b74d-aa3fe66f0f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-178271" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0$\n- ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})}$ is orthogonal\n- ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})}$ is orthonormal" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false since\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=3\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})⊥̸Q({u}_{3})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{3})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since the set is not even orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aafa25da-d701-5b8d-940d-a4b926749cbe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aafa25da-d701-5b8d-940d-a4b926749cbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "aafa25da-d701-5b8d-940d-a4b926749cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56148229-ce9a-5da3-a832-6f2fba7b9721" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d45cde3-2e6d-51fc-a005-c567ebefb006" "answer-26beaa3c-ed64-5711-ae43-5915ddfb5a17" "answer-b96f5746-2e70-560e-b999-9a3896073130" "answer-3400f53e-dd72-52d4-80f7-e75f042482c0" "answer-56148229-ce9a-5da3-a832-6f2fba7b9721"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d45cde3-2e6d-51fc-a005-c567ebefb006" :answer/id #uuid "7d45cde3-2e6d-51fc-a005-c567ebefb006" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26beaa3c-ed64-5711-ae43-5915ddfb5a17" :answer/id #uuid "26beaa3c-ed64-5711-ae43-5915ddfb5a17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b96f5746-2e70-560e-b999-9a3896073130" :answer/id #uuid "b96f5746-2e70-560e-b999-9a3896073130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3400f53e-dd72-52d4-80f7-e75f042482c0" :answer/id #uuid "3400f53e-dd72-52d4-80f7-e75f042482c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56148229-ce9a-5da3-a832-6f2fba7b9721" :answer/id #uuid "56148229-ce9a-5da3-a832-6f2fba7b9721" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8fec53f8-0962-53b9-8a63-104c832ed68f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8fec53f8-0962-53b9-8a63-104c832ed68f" :question/id #uuid "8fec53f8-0962-53b9-8a63-104c832ed68f" :question/math-academy-id "q-160710" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x-y,\\,v=x+y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the lines $x+y=1,$ $x-y=1$ and the curve ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x-y,\\,v=x+y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nSubstituting $x+y=v$ into the equation of the first line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y=1\\,⟹\\,v=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $x-y=u$ into the equation of the second line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y=1\\,⟹\\,u=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x+y=v$ and $x-y=u$ into the equation of curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2\\,⟹\\,(x-y)(x+y)=2,\\,⟹\\,uv=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection point of the two lines in the $uv$-plane is $(1,1).$\n\nTo find the intersection of the curve with the first line in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}uv=2 \\\\ v=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find the intersections of the curve with the second line in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}uv=2 \\\\ u=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the intersection points are $(1,1),$ $(1,2)$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,1\\le v\\le \\frac{2}{u}}.\n$$\n\n![](images/4c/4c151e7fc8d150b9c8def69d609446b77424c2703decd9c8c55866cff2ae7437.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\text{ }1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(2)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2/u}\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[v]_{1}^{2/u}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{2}{u}-1)du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡u-u]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e959dbb-ec9c-5316-8bef-b8459b6fb499"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e959dbb-ec9c-5316-8bef-b8459b6fb499" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e959dbb-ec9c-5316-8bef-b8459b6fb499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68da978e-5392-5c13-80d0-e709f72c6da6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e0953bd-cd3e-5daf-9baa-978871a2e773" "answer-a31dfc4c-cfac-5c12-8881-aa0d90cb5c66" "answer-5ea71a81-55b2-5821-a85d-2c2b860ef761" "answer-98fb62ce-1156-5b60-96a5-36d7a22956c9" "answer-68da978e-5392-5c13-80d0-e709f72c6da6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e0953bd-cd3e-5daf-9baa-978871a2e773" :answer/id #uuid "6e0953bd-cd3e-5daf-9baa-978871a2e773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a31dfc4c-cfac-5c12-8881-aa0d90cb5c66" :answer/id #uuid "a31dfc4c-cfac-5c12-8881-aa0d90cb5c66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ea71a81-55b2-5821-a85d-2c2b860ef761" :answer/id #uuid "5ea71a81-55b2-5821-a85d-2c2b860ef761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98fb62ce-1156-5b60-96a5-36d7a22956c9" :answer/id #uuid "98fb62ce-1156-5b60-96a5-36d7a22956c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68da978e-5392-5c13-80d0-e709f72c6da6" :answer/id #uuid "68da978e-5392-5c13-80d0-e709f72c6da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83d5f51e-5fd9-54c7-a184-30832a9e66a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83d5f51e-5fd9-54c7-a184-30832a9e66a8" :question/id #uuid "83d5f51e-5fd9-54c7-a184-30832a9e66a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109869" :question/problem "Consider a $11\\times 7$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=6,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=11,$ $n=7,$ and $m-r=6.$ \n\nSubstituting $m=11$ into $m-r=6,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(11)-r=6\\,⟹\\,r=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A)) & =r=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fbbcde84-7d88-5660-bb2d-2b1017fdef24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fbbcde84-7d88-5660-bb2d-2b1017fdef24" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbbcde84-7d88-5660-bb2d-2b1017fdef24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-085d1719-f1bf-5c7a-9e22-be69dfa7081a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a30bfe1f-d4e0-57ec-bbfc-86226618b689" "answer-d367a85e-2eaa-5ad0-8183-4f6dbec12d47" "answer-085d1719-f1bf-5c7a-9e22-be69dfa7081a" "answer-b1dec737-4c5a-52e5-87dc-5701ec98aa87" "answer-2a1cc760-8231-5baf-9a50-2bb58663a9ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a30bfe1f-d4e0-57ec-bbfc-86226618b689" :answer/id #uuid "a30bfe1f-d4e0-57ec-bbfc-86226618b689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d367a85e-2eaa-5ad0-8183-4f6dbec12d47" :answer/id #uuid "d367a85e-2eaa-5ad0-8183-4f6dbec12d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-085d1719-f1bf-5c7a-9e22-be69dfa7081a" :answer/id #uuid "085d1719-f1bf-5c7a-9e22-be69dfa7081a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1dec737-4c5a-52e5-87dc-5701ec98aa87" :answer/id #uuid "b1dec737-4c5a-52e5-87dc-5701ec98aa87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a1cc760-8231-5baf-9a50-2bb58663a9ab" :answer/id #uuid "2a1cc760-8231-5baf-9a50-2bb58663a9ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162093 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9a9c63b9-55aa-5f88-8ff0-b14dd8c3b850"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a9c63b9-55aa-5f88-8ff0-b14dd8c3b850" :question/id #uuid "9a9c63b9-55aa-5f88-8ff0-b14dd8c3b850" :question/math-academy-id "q-137889" :question/problem "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}17 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}17 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}[\\begin{aligned}-81 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4272bc52-3700-5a4c-920e-c054cf89452b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4272bc52-3700-5a4c-920e-c054cf89452b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4272bc52-3700-5a4c-920e-c054cf89452b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4d9f0f42-a4f1-5465-a3a2-7a60cda35ef3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d9f0f42-a4f1-5465-a3a2-7a60cda35ef3" "answer-118a9ee1-aa44-5777-9118-5227ee29fe39" "answer-343f47c9-bb05-5183-9f14-e8b4fa694501" "answer-fd063dda-be76-5f0e-93fe-6561f604b438" "answer-8cb4a560-b34c-5ecb-b912-d45e89d2bc34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d9f0f42-a4f1-5465-a3a2-7a60cda35ef3" :answer/id #uuid "4d9f0f42-a4f1-5465-a3a2-7a60cda35ef3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-118a9ee1-aa44-5777-9118-5227ee29fe39" :answer/id #uuid "118a9ee1-aa44-5777-9118-5227ee29fe39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-343f47c9-bb05-5183-9f14-e8b4fa694501" :answer/id #uuid "343f47c9-bb05-5183-9f14-e8b4fa694501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd063dda-be76-5f0e-93fe-6561f604b438" :answer/id #uuid "fd063dda-be76-5f0e-93fe-6561f604b438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cb4a560-b34c-5ecb-b912-d45e89d2bc34" :answer/id #uuid "8cb4a560-b34c-5ecb-b912-d45e89d2bc34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133765 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-10da4895-a162-564f-b4fa-20e4534242ed"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-10da4895-a162-564f-b4fa-20e4534242ed" :question/id #uuid "10da4895-a162-564f-b4fa-20e4534242ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-141044" :question/problem "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3+2i \\\\ 1-i \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2-i \\\\ 1+2i \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =(3+2i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{2-i})+(1-i)(\\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}})+3\\cdot \\overset{―}{2} \\\\  & =(3+2i)\\cdot (2+i)+(1-i)(1-2\\text{i})+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =(4+7i)+(-1-3\\text{i})+6 \\\\  & =9+4i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-daa09cb0-73ef-5ba1-8b3b-7e4c6c200a78"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-daa09cb0-73ef-5ba1-8b3b-7e4c6c200a78" :answer-field/id #uuid "daa09cb0-73ef-5ba1-8b3b-7e4c6c200a78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7fcb2432-46fc-5e27-b41d-7033f63e9a61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76bb0b0f-81de-5848-bca8-9f97f2642760" "answer-a8d0147c-c9d3-5bf2-9ee7-01acb39dd2f1" "answer-4176f4ff-1ff8-5626-b55e-5f7db3be26a7" "answer-d3e77397-1b64-592c-902d-00bf5998f038" "answer-7fcb2432-46fc-5e27-b41d-7033f63e9a61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76bb0b0f-81de-5848-bca8-9f97f2642760" :answer/id #uuid "76bb0b0f-81de-5848-bca8-9f97f2642760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11-2i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8d0147c-c9d3-5bf2-9ee7-01acb39dd2f1" :answer/id #uuid "a8d0147c-c9d3-5bf2-9ee7-01acb39dd2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11-4i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4176f4ff-1ff8-5626-b55e-5f7db3be26a7" :answer/id #uuid "4176f4ff-1ff8-5626-b55e-5f7db3be26a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13+2i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3e77397-1b64-592c-902d-00bf5998f038" :answer/id #uuid "d3e77397-1b64-592c-902d-00bf5998f038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fcb2432-46fc-5e27-b41d-7033f63e9a61" :answer/id #uuid "7fcb2432-46fc-5e27-b41d-7033f63e9a61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+4i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124597 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b34cb85d-113c-5f8c-bb3f-86df801d970e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b34cb85d-113c-5f8c-bb3f-86df801d970e" :question/id #uuid "b34cb85d-113c-5f8c-bb3f-86df801d970e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164552" :question/problem "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-6x-2z+8=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-6x-2z+8 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x)+4{y}^{2}-({z}^{2}+2z)+8 & =0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9+4{y}^{2}-(z+1)^{2}+1+8 & =0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+4{y}^{2}-(z+1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $(3,0,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dcd694e5-15ab-54db-83e7-909825ce1c4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcd694e5-15ab-54db-83e7-909825ce1c4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd694e5-15ab-54db-83e7-909825ce1c4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5618185e-e1f3-562e-9bda-391291612de3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b843362-d96d-5169-8747-167de74eaed4" "answer-383f6ed0-5fb4-59d2-b70a-efaec189d129" "answer-0171cec4-3060-54fe-b331-7b0cb56feb0e" "answer-5618185e-e1f3-562e-9bda-391291612de3" "answer-ebb80510-3271-536a-ba4e-07dbc48d8ccc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b843362-d96d-5169-8747-167de74eaed4" :answer/id #uuid "7b843362-d96d-5169-8747-167de74eaed4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(3,0,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-383f6ed0-5fb4-59d2-b70a-efaec189d129" :answer/id #uuid "383f6ed0-5fb4-59d2-b70a-efaec189d129" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(3,0,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0171cec4-3060-54fe-b331-7b0cb56feb0e" :answer/id #uuid "0171cec4-3060-54fe-b331-7b0cb56feb0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(-3,0,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5618185e-e1f3-562e-9bda-391291612de3" :answer/id #uuid "5618185e-e1f3-562e-9bda-391291612de3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(3,0,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebb80510-3271-536a-ba4e-07dbc48d8ccc" :answer/id #uuid "ebb80510-3271-536a-ba4e-07dbc48d8ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An elliptic cone centered at $(3,4,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166885 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5ff06561-72e7-5575-b3f6-d0740b1e717f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ff06561-72e7-5575-b3f6-d0740b1e717f" :question/id #uuid "5ff06561-72e7-5575-b3f6-d0740b1e717f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163259" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=4xy$ on the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $x\\ge 0$ and $y\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D:$ \n\n![](images/eb/eb8745d968da24a8500bd079638b17bc461ab2d97b93d1d1a7d6d4834365bb5a.png)\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA & ={∬}_{Δ}4(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}4{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{[{r}^{4}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{sin}^{2}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-89e7aed8-a1dc-58e4-8fb1-6b3e5ccc64a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89e7aed8-a1dc-58e4-8fb1-6b3e5ccc64a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "89e7aed8-a1dc-58e4-8fb1-6b3e5ccc64a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5bb3f282-1950-5f30-8116-34225566b739" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7eb342f1-4d9a-5fcf-8689-58e054ad9134" "answer-ce4175b2-aec8-519f-91bb-665c302224a2" "answer-f3fd7c58-8232-54be-81c8-be848ef0f965" "answer-50c3a6e2-38fd-585d-9e5e-4100891b13bd" "answer-5bb3f282-1950-5f30-8116-34225566b739"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7eb342f1-4d9a-5fcf-8689-58e054ad9134" :answer/id #uuid "7eb342f1-4d9a-5fcf-8689-58e054ad9134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce4175b2-aec8-519f-91bb-665c302224a2" :answer/id #uuid "ce4175b2-aec8-519f-91bb-665c302224a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3fd7c58-8232-54be-81c8-be848ef0f965" :answer/id #uuid "f3fd7c58-8232-54be-81c8-be848ef0f965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50c3a6e2-38fd-585d-9e5e-4100891b13bd" :answer/id #uuid "50c3a6e2-38fd-585d-9e5e-4100891b13bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bb3f282-1950-5f30-8116-34225566b739" :answer/id #uuid "5bb3f282-1950-5f30-8116-34225566b739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198395 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea08d184-a351-56ae-9a07-8c580e0db18b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea08d184-a351-56ae-9a07-8c580e0db18b" :question/id #uuid "ea08d184-a351-56ae-9a07-8c580e0db18b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161478" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9a66f9263c9009f634668e826f0a84320103589b9c270360d7b2465c71e74592.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}2xz\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/49/49a3333a52a6b7d7451095dbc46ab1009df491c92726436929a6f93cff38db60.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3-2x},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/df/dfa0a80bc323401f050d1302dc42c92558d8b566d9b0f985e955d34eb5cc15bd.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3-2x}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xz\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-2x}2xz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-2x}2xz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-2x}2xz\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=3-2x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(3-2x)^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(9x-12{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(9x-12{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(9x-12{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3})\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9x-12{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}){[y]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2(9x-12{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(18x-24{x}^{2}+8{x}^{3})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(18x-24{x}^{2}+8{x}^{3})\\,dx & ={[9{x}^{2}-8{x}^{3}+2{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =[9-8+2] \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c98ba671-2bb4-5d19-af70-c7ece3f49aad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c98ba671-2bb4-5d19-af70-c7ece3f49aad" :answer-field/id #uuid "c98ba671-2bb4-5d19-af70-c7ece3f49aad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48500948-cdb6-529b-a0bc-286d87402c18" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44134047-b619-5b75-95ac-b0b768bfc280" "answer-74b03522-30b1-5e12-8b2f-401801548125" "answer-a856eea2-f4ed-56ad-86b9-3283ac5168a2" "answer-48500948-cdb6-529b-a0bc-286d87402c18" "answer-bd5b372b-f330-5a9d-ba39-457635409bc5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44134047-b619-5b75-95ac-b0b768bfc280" :answer/id #uuid "44134047-b619-5b75-95ac-b0b768bfc280" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74b03522-30b1-5e12-8b2f-401801548125" :answer/id #uuid "74b03522-30b1-5e12-8b2f-401801548125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a856eea2-f4ed-56ad-86b9-3283ac5168a2" :answer/id #uuid "a856eea2-f4ed-56ad-86b9-3283ac5168a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48500948-cdb6-529b-a0bc-286d87402c18" :answer/id #uuid "48500948-cdb6-529b-a0bc-286d87402c18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd5b372b-f330-5a9d-ba39-457635409bc5" :answer/id #uuid "bd5b372b-f330-5a9d-ba39-457635409bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231590 :question/problem "Find the solution $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+3{y}^{′}(t)+2y(t)={u}_{2}(t),\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+3sY(s)+2Y(s)=\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=u(t-2)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-(t-2)}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+3sY(s)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+3s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ (s+1)(s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & ={e}^{-2s}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse transform, we first use partial fraction decomposition on the algebraic part:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{s(s+1)(s+2)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{s+1}+\\frac{C}{s+2}\n$$\n\nSolving for the constants, we find $A=\\frac{1}{2}$, $B=-1$, and $C=\\frac{1}{2}$, giving:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+3s+2)}=\\frac{1}{2s}-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{2(s+2)}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the inverse Laplace transform. Let \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{1}{2s}-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{2(s+2)},\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nf(t)=\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-t}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the second shifting theorem, \n\n$$\n{L}^{-1}{{e}^{-as}F(s)}={u}_{a}(t)f(t-a).\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{e}^{-2s}F(s)} \\\\ y(t) & ={u}_{2}(t)\\,f(t-2) \\\\ y(t) & =u(t-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-{e}^{-(t-2)}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2(t-2)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-12db3d9d-3cba-5ebb-a53d-3149d14faf15"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12db3d9d-3cba-5ebb-a53d-3149d14faf15" :answer-field/id #uuid "12db3d9d-3cba-5ebb-a53d-3149d14faf15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0f87f2fe-f5bd-58d0-8229-020d3f04a17d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f87f2fe-f5bd-58d0-8229-020d3f04a17d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f87f2fe-f5bd-58d0-8229-020d3f04a17d" :answer/id #uuid "0f87f2fe-f5bd-58d0-8229-020d3f04a17d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e^{-2(t-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-58242fe6-4f94-5872-a2af-27a25e52256a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-58242fe6-4f94-5872-a2af-27a25e52256a" :question/id #uuid "58242fe6-4f94-5872-a2af-27a25e52256a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124278" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d83f771aa650879909c33d7033e80ca044b7e6f8369e19667e6173aa8a40737.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}(x+\\sqrt{3y})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(2,0)$ and $(0,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(2+t(0-2)),\\,(0+t(3-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-2t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+\\sqrt{3y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2-2t)+\\sqrt{3(3t)} \\\\  & =2-2t+3\\sqrt{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-2t+3\\sqrt{t})\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-2t+3{t}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{[2t-{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3[(2(1)-(1)^{2}+2(1)^{3/2})-(0)] \\\\  & =3(3) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5ed96f7f-49a8-554d-a91d-a5525992b220"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ed96f7f-49a8-554d-a91d-a5525992b220" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed96f7f-49a8-554d-a91d-a5525992b220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fbdd4223-88ec-5c0a-a0b3-1dc095b07709" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18b329fb-ed63-5c9c-ba4f-1ae88547c789" "answer-c32ac31a-d68d-5bbe-8d37-51261f4658fe" "answer-3565a038-62ce-5c59-8e95-c3505e80c675" "answer-46436b71-8e85-5a39-bf27-5ed0f753e896" "answer-fbdd4223-88ec-5c0a-a0b3-1dc095b07709"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18b329fb-ed63-5c9c-ba4f-1ae88547c789" :answer/id #uuid "18b329fb-ed63-5c9c-ba4f-1ae88547c789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c32ac31a-d68d-5bbe-8d37-51261f4658fe" :answer/id #uuid "c32ac31a-d68d-5bbe-8d37-51261f4658fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3565a038-62ce-5c59-8e95-c3505e80c675" :answer/id #uuid "3565a038-62ce-5c59-8e95-c3505e80c675" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46436b71-8e85-5a39-bf27-5ed0f753e896" :answer/id #uuid "46436b71-8e85-5a39-bf27-5ed0f753e896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdd4223-88ec-5c0a-a0b3-1dc095b07709" :answer/id #uuid "fbdd4223-88ec-5c0a-a0b3-1dc095b07709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72" :question/id #uuid "1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72" :question/math-academy-id "q-147946" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{9}{16},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y[\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}-(\\frac{5}{4})(\\frac{9}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" "answer-e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" "answer-f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" "answer-964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" "answer-a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" :answer/id #uuid "c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" :answer/id #uuid "f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" :answer/id #uuid "964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b" :answer/id #uuid "a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-409399cd-9cd7-53bb-83f5-ffa99003572c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-409399cd-9cd7-53bb-83f5-ffa99003572c" :question/id #uuid "409399cd-9cd7-53bb-83f5-ffa99003572c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95407" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is a real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ must have a complex eigenvalue\n- $A$ is not diagonalizable\n- If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, so, $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7ab4e9c4-6a2c-5be8-9bcf-e0683aaf1263"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7ab4e9c4-6a2c-5be8-9bcf-e0683aaf1263" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab4e9c4-6a2c-5be8-9bcf-e0683aaf1263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5343ac3-3229-5247-ba18-b96c1194c0cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0cc8f06-8966-54df-b620-04802f29078b" "answer-5bd70172-7256-5614-bf05-3767b88a1cba" "answer-a1851ac1-51c2-53a9-b604-327eb8a7e44b" "answer-adec6066-5ccc-5ce4-bd6d-a02f3d4d86ed" "answer-c5343ac3-3229-5247-ba18-b96c1194c0cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0cc8f06-8966-54df-b620-04802f29078b" :answer/id #uuid "c0cc8f06-8966-54df-b620-04802f29078b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd70172-7256-5614-bf05-3767b88a1cba" :answer/id #uuid "5bd70172-7256-5614-bf05-3767b88a1cba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1851ac1-51c2-53a9-b604-327eb8a7e44b" :answer/id #uuid "a1851ac1-51c2-53a9-b604-327eb8a7e44b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adec6066-5ccc-5ce4-bd6d-a02f3d4d86ed" :answer/id #uuid "adec6066-5ccc-5ce4-bd6d-a02f3d4d86ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5343ac3-3229-5247-ba18-b96c1194c0cf" :answer/id #uuid "c5343ac3-3229-5247-ba18-b96c1194c0cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172134 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e4bd89e0-666c-5b6d-a3d4-7d170f1093d4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4bd89e0-666c-5b6d-a3d4-7d170f1093d4" :question/id #uuid "e4bd89e0-666c-5b6d-a3d4-7d170f1093d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-162818" :question/problem "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=x-2y-2z$ on the intersection of the plane $x+y+z=2$ and the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x-2y-2z\n$$\n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=x+y+z=2,\\,h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y,z)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y,z)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=2 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by expanding the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,-2,-2⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨1,1,1⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,0,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}1=\\lambda +2\\mu x \\\\ -2=\\lambda  \\\\ -2=\\lambda +2\\mu z\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{3}{2\\mu } \\\\ \\lambda =-2 \\\\ \\mu z=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\mu $ can't be zero since this leads to a contradiction. So, from the third equation above, we must have $z=0.$\n\nNext, we substitute $z=0$  into the second constraint:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we substitute $x$ and $z$ into the first constraint:\n\n- If $x=1$ and $z=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & =2 \\\\ 1+y+0 & =2 \\\\ 1+y & =2 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x=-1$ and $z=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & =2 \\\\ -1+y+0 & =2 \\\\ -1+y & =2 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(1,1,0),\\,(-1,3,0).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y,z)$ | $(1,1,0)$ | $(-1,3,0)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y,z)$ | $-1$ | $-7$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at $(-1,3,0),$ and its  minimum value is $-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a18338f5-cccd-53a6-b949-c33ab13e3ef2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a18338f5-cccd-53a6-b949-c33ab13e3ef2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a18338f5-cccd-53a6-b949-c33ab13e3ef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4a6381f4-a213-5d2b-a1cc-2cec4867e43d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bdc80792-2d44-5042-bdf5-ee15cb21d305" "answer-f4841998-b430-5860-99e4-67399dd743f0" "answer-4a6381f4-a213-5d2b-a1cc-2cec4867e43d" "answer-9a843324-4732-5b29-8d8d-9057bdddcade" "answer-24445614-cbdd-51e8-9c4a-2bb44029ae1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdc80792-2d44-5042-bdf5-ee15cb21d305" :answer/id #uuid "bdc80792-2d44-5042-bdf5-ee15cb21d305" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4841998-b430-5860-99e4-67399dd743f0" :answer/id #uuid "f4841998-b430-5860-99e4-67399dd743f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a6381f4-a213-5d2b-a1cc-2cec4867e43d" :answer/id #uuid "4a6381f4-a213-5d2b-a1cc-2cec4867e43d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a843324-4732-5b29-8d8d-9057bdddcade" :answer/id #uuid "9a843324-4732-5b29-8d8d-9057bdddcade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24445614-cbdd-51e8-9c4a-2bb44029ae1d" :answer/id #uuid "24445614-cbdd-51e8-9c4a-2bb44029ae1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083255 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-54a3ad17-4b32-5c5c-9805-6f8326875645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-54a3ad17-4b32-5c5c-9805-6f8326875645" :question/id #uuid "54a3ad17-4b32-5c5c-9805-6f8326875645" :question/math-academy-id "q-75348" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations in the domain $[0,\\pi )$, so this is the only value of $t$ when the object is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6dd3c36c-4848-5d1c-aa76-d8c668fd16df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6dd3c36c-4848-5d1c-aa76-d8c668fd16df" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd3c36c-4848-5d1c-aa76-d8c668fd16df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76d03abe-342f-5856-88ef-14d38dc18a0b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84c8ef99-9d06-5ddb-b760-2f1f8d324604" "answer-239aab55-cf5b-57dc-825b-cb5831c86600" "answer-b55d3522-25ff-5c55-a36e-d0d705ae61d4" "answer-76d03abe-342f-5856-88ef-14d38dc18a0b" "answer-613f0aa8-03f2-5c51-a570-bdaf7627215c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c8ef99-9d06-5ddb-b760-2f1f8d324604" :answer/id #uuid "84c8ef99-9d06-5ddb-b760-2f1f8d324604" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-239aab55-cf5b-57dc-825b-cb5831c86600" :answer/id #uuid "239aab55-cf5b-57dc-825b-cb5831c86600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b55d3522-25ff-5c55-a36e-d0d705ae61d4" :answer/id #uuid "b55d3522-25ff-5c55-a36e-d0d705ae61d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76d03abe-342f-5856-88ef-14d38dc18a0b" :answer/id #uuid "76d03abe-342f-5856-88ef-14d38dc18a0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-613f0aa8-03f2-5c51-a570-bdaf7627215c" :answer/id #uuid "613f0aa8-03f2-5c51-a570-bdaf7627215c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0bdbb35e-75fd-595e-96b4-a35903811dc9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0bdbb35e-75fd-595e-96b4-a35903811dc9" :question/id #uuid "0bdbb35e-75fd-595e-96b4-a35903811dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-82288" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}7 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 14 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 14 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|B|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1fee267d-6a43-5586-8b7a-525bf46d0281"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1fee267d-6a43-5586-8b7a-525bf46d0281" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fee267d-6a43-5586-8b7a-525bf46d0281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" :answer-field/choices ["answer-119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" "answer-6ba19205-12b7-5ea8-b9b0-c94f0fbef5be" "answer-52d15588-08f4-5de2-baf0-27c5fa69cb33" "answer-6657d1d7-2317-536b-a73c-9536580d61e5" "answer-c92f219d-fedf-5abc-84b3-73dbff86703f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" :answer/id #uuid "119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ba19205-12b7-5ea8-b9b0-c94f0fbef5be" :answer/id #uuid "6ba19205-12b7-5ea8-b9b0-c94f0fbef5be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52d15588-08f4-5de2-baf0-27c5fa69cb33" :answer/id #uuid "52d15588-08f4-5de2-baf0-27c5fa69cb33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6657d1d7-2317-536b-a73c-9536580d61e5" :answer/id #uuid "6657d1d7-2317-536b-a73c-9536580d61e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c92f219d-fedf-5abc-84b3-73dbff86703f" :answer/id #uuid "c92f219d-fedf-5abc-84b3-73dbff86703f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e36b6ce2-87d8-527f-bbbc-2bd96f3e28ba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e36b6ce2-87d8-527f-bbbc-2bd96f3e28ba" :question/id #uuid "e36b6ce2-87d8-527f-bbbc-2bd96f3e28ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-96955" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.01.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.3263)=0.99.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.3263)=1-0.99=0.01.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.3263)=0.01.\n$$\n\n![](images/22/2212ee9de7a440c5d61814d1b2b50a249849756a4aa331e4f48180c67f95944f.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.3263) & =0.01 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.3263) & =0.01.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.3263.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1d9ce56-1f33-5833-970c-b90417bb5185"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1d9ce56-1f33-5833-970c-b90417bb5185" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1d9ce56-1f33-5833-970c-b90417bb5185" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c032ac6a-191f-50e9-b774-d3ba8a0aa31a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13de821a-673d-52a1-abb8-221370b7644e" "answer-c032ac6a-191f-50e9-b774-d3ba8a0aa31a" "answer-b1de25e6-7a35-5ea9-8805-939d49cdada4" "answer-980f7d94-bf9b-589b-ad6f-1076c430f850" "answer-bbf5e1c0-cbfb-5adf-8e13-b28cc1b2990c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13de821a-673d-52a1-abb8-221370b7644e" :answer/id #uuid "13de821a-673d-52a1-abb8-221370b7644e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c032ac6a-191f-50e9-b774-d3ba8a0aa31a" :answer/id #uuid "c032ac6a-191f-50e9-b774-d3ba8a0aa31a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.3263" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1de25e6-7a35-5ea9-8805-939d49cdada4" :answer/id #uuid "b1de25e6-7a35-5ea9-8805-939d49cdada4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-980f7d94-bf9b-589b-ad6f-1076c430f850" :answer/id #uuid "980f7d94-bf9b-589b-ad6f-1076c430f850" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2816" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbf5e1c0-cbfb-5adf-8e13-b28cc1b2990c" :answer/id #uuid "bbf5e1c0-cbfb-5adf-8e13-b28cc1b2990c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3263" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157384 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07ccf333-53bd-54f7-b1d6-69a0bfd5212a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-07ccf333-53bd-54f7-b1d6-69a0bfd5212a" :question/id #uuid "07ccf333-53bd-54f7-b1d6-69a0bfd5212a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109507" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[1-4X].$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find $\\text{E}[X].$ \n\nThe expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0.05-3\\cdot 0.1-2\\cdot 0.15-1\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[1-4X] & =\\text{E}[-4X+1] \\\\  & =-4\\text{E}[X]+1 \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (-1)+1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-460301a7-dfff-537c-a411-380314c66618"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-460301a7-dfff-537c-a411-380314c66618" :answer-field/id #uuid "460301a7-dfff-537c-a411-380314c66618" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-377ddaef-26c1-5184-9404-c9f13bfe03ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5009fd9-ab4c-5109-bdbe-4f83082d55cf" "answer-e944144d-5148-5cae-8f11-5f7ccf81f260" "answer-98610e3b-03bb-5bfc-82c5-55956cfa7feb" "answer-7eb4a396-0211-5762-983d-45ad03555645" "answer-377ddaef-26c1-5184-9404-c9f13bfe03ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5009fd9-ab4c-5109-bdbe-4f83082d55cf" :answer/id #uuid "d5009fd9-ab4c-5109-bdbe-4f83082d55cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e944144d-5148-5cae-8f11-5f7ccf81f260" :answer/id #uuid "e944144d-5148-5cae-8f11-5f7ccf81f260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98610e3b-03bb-5bfc-82c5-55956cfa7feb" :answer/id #uuid "98610e3b-03bb-5bfc-82c5-55956cfa7feb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7eb4a396-0211-5762-983d-45ad03555645" :answer/id #uuid "7eb4a396-0211-5762-983d-45ad03555645" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-377ddaef-26c1-5184-9404-c9f13bfe03ed" :answer/id #uuid "377ddaef-26c1-5184-9404-c9f13bfe03ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186396318 :question/problem "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{b(t)}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{t}b(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308522 :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(1)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with two steps to approximate $y(2)$ and ${y}^{′}(2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314869 :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166959 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-28e99078-3ec4-5f03-89e8-002bc319270f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-28e99078-3ec4-5f03-89e8-002bc319270f" :question/id #uuid "28e99078-3ec4-5f03-89e8-002bc319270f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341261" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=2x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{n}.$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=2x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-1)}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{4((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3c0f520-1723-59a6-8809-23fd43dd82d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3c0f520-1723-59a6-8809-23fd43dd82d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c0f520-1723-59a6-8809-23fd43dd82d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-7eb6d1b1-e270-50cc-b737-a42a196ea497" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8072e196-2965-5a76-9a1d-d9efca253043" "answer-cf616d92-23e4-5fcc-aa08-dc8557e3b8bf" "answer-3a2fa8da-c552-58ab-a33e-0bb1c7ad9d86" "answer-7eb6d1b1-e270-50cc-b737-a42a196ea497" "answer-b40acf84-64c2-5c56-ae91-e946666f2e3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8072e196-2965-5a76-9a1d-d9efca253043" :answer/id #uuid "8072e196-2965-5a76-9a1d-d9efca253043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf616d92-23e4-5fcc-aa08-dc8557e3b8bf" :answer/id #uuid "cf616d92-23e4-5fcc-aa08-dc8557e3b8bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a2fa8da-c552-58ab-a33e-0bb1c7ad9d86" :answer/id #uuid "3a2fa8da-c552-58ab-a33e-0bb1c7ad9d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7eb6d1b1-e270-50cc-b737-a42a196ea497" :answer/id #uuid "7eb6d1b1-e270-50cc-b737-a42a196ea497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b40acf84-64c2-5c56-ae91-e946666f2e3d" :answer/id #uuid "b40acf84-64c2-5c56-ae91-e946666f2e3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4(1+(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186397263 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=y(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308409 :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85b327bb-322d-5a68-8a63-58e73227920b" "answer-field-2eca90ea-6e9d-54ce-929c-c17c1f8b5fd7" "answer-field-0acbd359-